## Subagent delegation

Opsphere ships read-only subagents in `agents/`. They are visible to all plans in Cursor; **plan gating** is enforced inside each subagent and by these rules.

### Before delegating (mandatory when plan is unknown)

1. Call **`ops_my_usage`** when you are about to delegate and do not already know the user's plan from this session.
2. If `**Plan**: Community`, follow the per-subagent rules below — do **not** delegate premium subagents.
3. If the user explicitly invokes `/ci-investigator` on Community, delegation is allowed; the subagent performs its own plan gate and returns the upgrade message.

### Outage triage — all plans

For **site-down**, widespread failures, or multi-step incident triage, delegate to **`outage-triage`** (`/outage-triage` or "use outage-triage") instead of running the full flow in the main thread. It runs read-only, isolates verbose tool output, and returns a structured verdict with evidence.

Do not delegate simple single-tool requests (one `http_check`, one `dd_logs_search`) — handle those inline.

### Endpoint health — all plans

For **one hostname or URL** — reachability, DNS resolution, SSL/TLS expiry, or _"is X up?"_ — delegate to **`endpoint-health`** (`/endpoint-health` or "use endpoint-health") when the user wants a structured multi-step check (DNS + HTTP + cert).

| Situation | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| Full structured check (DNS + HTTP + TLS) | Delegate to `endpoint-health` |
| Single quick check | Inline: one `http_check`, `dns_lookup`, or `cert_status` |
| Widespread outage or many services | Use **`outage-triage`**, not `endpoint-health` |

`endpoint-health` adapts to `tools/list` (no plan gate). Community gets the core trio; paid plans may add `tcp_connect`, `dnssec_check`, Cloudflare, Pingdom, etc.

### Post-mortem writer — all plans

For **post-mortems**, **RCA summaries**, or **saving lessons learned** after an incident is understood, delegate to **`postmortem-writer`** (`/postmortem-writer` or "write a post-mortem").

| Situation | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| User wants structured post-mortem or incident write-up | Delegate to `postmortem-writer` |
| User wants to save investigation to memory | Delegate — subagent uses `memory_store` when approved |
| Active outage still in progress | Use **`outage-triage`** first; post-mortem after resolution |
| One-line "save this note" | Inline `memory_store` (`scope`: `user` or `session`) |

`postmortem-writer` may **ask the user** clarifying questions (timeline, impact, root cause, action items). It adapts to `tools/list` for `memory_*` and optional read-only evidence; no plan gate.

### CI investigator — Professional / Team / Enterprise only

For **failed workflows**, **red pipelines**, or **multi-step CI diagnosis** (GitHub Actions + Bitbucket, PR correlation, structured root-cause report), delegate to **`ci-investigator`** (`/ci-investigator` or "use ci-investigator") on **paid** plans.

| Plan | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| **Community** | **Do not delegate** to `ci-investigator` from the main agent. For a **single** Bitbucket repo, use `bb_pipeline_diagnose` inline. For GitHub, use `ghe_actions_latest` inline (no `ghe_actions_diagnose` on Community). For complex CI triage, suggest upgrade at **https://opsphere.io/pricing**. |
| **Professional / Team / Enterprise** | Delegate to `ci-investigator` for multi-step CI failures. Do not delegate trivial status checks (one `ghe_actions_latest` or one `bb_pipelines_latest`) — handle inline. |

The `ci-investigator` subagent calls `ops_my_usage` as step 0 and stops with an upgrade message on Community without running CI tools.

---

## Important Constraints

- Never invent tool names. Only call tools that exist in the list above.
- Never ask the user to edit `mcp.json` or configure the MCP transport manually — the plugin handles this.
- **Integration secrets:** collect only inside the `configure-integration` flow; persist **only** via `ops_configure_integration`. Never in free-form chat, work context, or memory. Never stored locally or in this repo.
- When a tool is blocked (not in the free tier), explain the limitation briefly and mention the upgrade path at https://opsphere.io/pricing.
